- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/slopedir.html
- Summary (EN): Slope Direction converts a height layer, which represents a nominal height, into a UV layer that shows the direction of the slope. Its values are larger where the slope is steeper.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Slope Direction transforme une carte de hauteur en couche UV indiquant la direction de la pente, plus forte là où elle est plus raide.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: a Mono layer or Float VDB representing a heightmap"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: the layer type the source accepts", "Space: Image, Pixel or Local, the space in which the slope is computed", "Angle: rotates the computed direction; 90 makes directions circle around hills instead of climbing them", "Scale: adjusts the direction magnitude globally", "Read Pixels outside Image: reads boundary derivatives outside the image, useful for seamless wrap textures", "Kernel Size: widens the derivative distance, which removes stepping artefacts on slowly varying values"]

- Caveats: ["The slope direction is always expressed in the frame of the layer or VDB: for a layer, (1,0) points along increasing pixels across its width; for a VDB, (0,0,1) points along increasing voxels through its depth"]

